is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: switch4
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Campus 2 access switch “switch4,” specifically the VLAN 5 uplink/trunk subinterface eth0.5 (Linux VLAN interface bridged into br_vlan5).

Mechanism: PCs in VLAN 5 can communicate locally (e.g., pc1 -> pc2 succeeds), but cannot reach their default gateway 10.5.0.254 on the core switch because VLAN 5 traffic cannot traverse the uplink to sshswitch. This manifests as “Destination Host Unreachable” and failed ARP resolution to the gateway from both sides.

Localization: On switch4, eth0.5 (the tagged VLAN 5 subinterface on the uplink eth0 toward sshswitch) is administratively DOWN and in bridge_slave “disabled” state, while eth0.6 (VLAN 6) is UP and forwarding. Evidence:
- pc1 has correct IP and default route; ping 10.5.0.254 fails with “Destination Host Unreachable,” while ping to 10.5.0.2 (same VLAN) works.
- switch4: “ip -d link show eth0.5” shows state DOWN, master br_vlan5, bridge_slave state disabled; “eth0.6” is UP/forwarding.
- sshswitch: eth0.5 is UP and in br_v5 (10.5.0.254), but ping to 10.5.0.1 also returns “Destination Host Unreachable,” confirming the break is on the switch4 side of the trunk for VLAN 5.

Root cause: VLAN 5 trunk subinterface eth0.5 on switch4 is administratively down, preventing VLAN 5 frames from reaching the gateway.

Corrective fix: Bring up eth0.5 and ensure it remains enslaved to br_vlan5 (e.g., “ip link set dev eth0.5 up” and persist via config). Verify both ends tag VLAN 5 on the ms1_sw4 trunk. After enabling, ARP to 10.5.0.254 should succeed and VLAN 5 reachability will be restored. === END ===